{"game": "arma-3", "language": "english", "appid": 107410, "month": "2021-05", "window": 4, "start_date": 1621814400, "end_date": 1622505599, "month_true_total": 1961, "quota": 5, "returned": 5, "pulled_at": "2026-10-09 11:13:13 UTC", "reviews": [{"recommendationid": "92962703", "author": {"steamid": "76561198868731017", "personaname": "Dayvox", "persona_status": "offline", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/id/62318123/", "num_games_owned": 0, "num_reviews": 18, "playtime_forever": 2501, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 2501, "last_played": 1588357086, "avatar": "85c3bd6a6a7ab4f7670e86fbae79d83624e21391"}, "language": "english", "review": "She and I have returned from a holiday back-packing (well, case-pulling) around Albania. We went the length of the country, catching buses from town to town and finding somewhere to stay when we arrived.\n\nI wanted to again see a European country much as I remember them in the early 60s before everything became the same, with same shops and similar food, and that's pretty much what we found. Albania is family-centred, safe, respectable and amazingly cheap; two people can eat with a drink for £5 and eat like royalty for £15.\n\nEvery evening, families and friends get dressed up and go promenading up and down the main street. It's a young society with few fat people and is untouched by the Americans (we didn't see a single McDonalds in the whole country).\n\nSo, if you can survive a run-down infrastructure and customer-blindness, you could try a holiday in Albania. It has wonderful scenery, beach resorts and important archaeology.", "timestamp_created": 1622504257, "timestamp_updated": 1622504257, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 0, "votes_funny": 1, "weighted_vote_score": 0.5, "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": false, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1378969200", "reactions": []}, {"recommendationid":